{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0536","billNumberShort":"H.B. 536","billNumberLong":"HB0536S02","fileNumber":"2026FL1435","shortTitle":"Criminal Conduct on Public Lands Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"BARLOSE","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Barlow, Stewart E.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"IPSONDL","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Ipson, Don L.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill concerns criminal conduct on public lands.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>creates the Public Lands Restoration and Protection Fund (fund) to be administered by the State Historic Preservation Office;<hr><ltbullet>amends the criminal offense of defacing by graffiti on public lands, including to add conduct involving natural and archaeological features;<hr><ltbullet>amends penalty provisions for certain criminal violations of the offense of antiquities alteration, removal, injury, or destruction;<hr><ltbullet>provides that a court may order criminal restitution to be deposited into the fund for a violation of:<hr><ltbullet1>defacing by graffiti, damage, or destruction on public lands; or<hr><ltbullet1>antiquities alteration, removal, injury, or destruction, if the violation is on state lands; and <hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Jackie Rogers","fiscalAnalyst":"Laurie Haupt","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"YEQWGXWTHP","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-10 14:06:20.177","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and Gen